    <DataNode elementId="Glucopyranose" textLabel="D-glucopyranose" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="WQZGKKKJIJFFOK-GASJEMHNSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="855.7607421875" centerY="977.35595703125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">This compound stands for a mixture of |FRAME: ALPHA-GLUCOSE| and |FRAME: GLC|. In most cases, each of these compounds mutarotates quickly to form a mixture of the two, and thus it is the general rule to use this non-specific form in reactions unless it is specifically known that an enzyme can accept only one of the forms.</Comment>
