    <DataNode elementId="Malto-Oligosaccharides" textLabel="a maltooligosaccharide" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="17593" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="1077.034912109375" centerY="786.93896484375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>Maltooligosaccharides are glucooligosaccharides derived from D-glucose monomers linked via &amp;alpha;-1,4 bonds as in |FRAME: MALTOSE|. More specifically, the term is applied to linear oligosaccharides composed of more than two and less than ten units of glucose. The corresponding &amp;alpha;-1,6 glucooligosaccharides are called |FRAME: Isomaltooligosaccharides isomaltooligosaccharides|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="Malto-Oligosaccharides" />
